PLOP3        ---- 100 000011100
# 0x80d, which neither NAK nor CuAssembler's sm_86 list has: by the name, PSETP ("Combine Predicates and Set
# Predicate"), which NVIDIA's Ampere instruction set table lists in the predicate group beside PLOP3 (0x81c) and which
# compute compilers don't emit. An Ounce game's vertex programs end with two of them after six FSETPs of the position
# against its w (P0 to P5, outside each clip plane), then @P0 EXIT before any output is written: a cull test of the
# vertex. Its destinations are at bits 81 and 84 as PLOP3's (both PT in the first, P0 in the second); bits 32-63 hold
# 0xc4321111 in the first and 0x80000000 in the second, by their nibbles the predicate operands (not decoded). Only
# this form is seen
PSETP        ---- 100 000001101
UPLOP3       ---- 100 010011100
CS2R         ---- 100 000000101
S2R          ---- 100 100011001
S2UR         ---- 100 111000011
R2UR         ---- 001 111000010
# NAK encodes UMOV as a uniform ALU instruction: form 4 an immediate (0x882), form 6 a uniform register (0xc82)
UMOV         ---- 100 010000010
UMOV         ---- 110 010000010
REDUX        ---- 001 111000100
VOTE         ---- 100 000000110
UVOTE        ---- 100 010000110
MATCH        ---- 001 110100001
SHFL_RR      ---- 001 110001001
SHFL_RI      ---- 010 110001001
SHFL_IR      ---- 100 110001001
SHFL_II      ---- 111 110001001
